                <pb facs="0213" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg179"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The UNC and Communist Delegates convened in
                    plenary session at 11 a.m. on April 28, 1952. The UNC Delegate expressed his intention to propose an overall
                    settlement in executive session. Following a 30-minute recess, the Communist
                    Delegate agreed to go into executive session. The UNC Delegate, Admiral Joy,
                    made his statement (for text, see telegram C 67603, Ridgway to JCS, April 26, <ref
                        target="#pg173">page 173</ref>) which was duly noted by the Communist
                    Delegate, General Nam Il, who asked for
                    another short recess until 2:30 p.m. Following this recess, General Nam stated, “Our side fails to see how
                    your proposal this morning can really be of help to an overall settlement of the
                    remaining issues.” Nam then called for a
                    recess. Joy made the final statement
                    before adjournment <pb facs="0214" n="180" xml:id="pg180"/> of the session when
                    he reemphasized that the UNC offer was its
                    “final and irrevocable effort.” Thus the “Package Proposal” was delivered. A
                    record of the substance of this session, in telegram C 67677, Ridgway to JCS, April 28, 1952, is in FE files, lot
                    55 D 128, tab 87.</p>
            </div>
